# {{ name }}

A Python service reached by [`laranail/python`](https://opensource.simtabi.com/documentation/laranail/python/).

## Run it

```bash
python -m venv .venv && . .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
uvicorn main:app --reload --port {{ port }}
```

## Wire it up

```php
// config/laranail/python.php
'services' => [
    '{{ name }}' => [
        'base_url' => env('PYTHON_{{ NAME }}_URL', 'http://127.0.0.1:{{ port }}'),
    ],
],
```

Then `php artisan laranail::python.doctor` to confirm it answers.

## The three contracts

| | Must be |
|---|---|
| `/health` | `{"status": "healthy"}` — or change `health_key`/`healthy_value` to match |
| Callback signature | HMAC-SHA256 over `"{timestamp}.{raw_body}"`, header `X-Laranail-Signature: sha256=<hex>` |
| Callback secret | `PYTHON_CALLBACK_SECRET`, matching `laranail.python.callbacks.secrets[0]` |

Sign the **raw bytes you send**. Serialising twice — once to sign, once to send —
is how signatures start failing for payloads containing non-ASCII.
